 "notes": {
  "labels": "Joe (2026-09-28): the ten brands are bottles with their logos on the back bar, and the bottles should stand out with our logos. Draft b1 drew the ten bottles well but garbled several labels (GREY COOSE, CAMAEERNA, WHITEEY). Every label is repainted from the brand's own logo file (art/references/local/brands/, ignored): each keeps the draft's rectangle, filled flat with the logo's ground, the logo drawn at 8x and reduced. Grey Goose and RumChata are printed on the glass, so the old print is cleared to the bottle's own column colours first. Lettering under about 6 px garbles in the 4x upscale, so GREY GOOSE and NEW AMSTERDAM are stacked a word a line, small words are thickened, New Amsterdam's and Camarena's labels widen to the glass edges with their letters heightened, and VODKA and TEQUILA are left off. AMSTERDAM (nine letters in 33 px) still reads only as a line of lettering.",
  "sign": "Joe (2026-09-28): on the door of the cooler behind the right bar, a circular sign like draft a2's round plaques, carrying the Side Project light-bulb logo; clicking it grants the beer mug. Painted at 8x: a disc of radius 35 centred on the door slab between its top strap hinge and its handle, a dark brown rim, a cream face, a thin inner ring and the Side Project logo (script and bulb, from the brewery's logo file) in the logo's own brown, with a soft shadow down-right on the door."
 }
